From 5a504c09925768da5263a98db05ac1c0b30d99c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Braun <sam@webry.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:44:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): the operation as a gray tag at the bottom of the
 file list

REBASE, MERGE, CHERRY-PICK, ... in muted small caps text; the hover
keeps the full line and the commit message, the accessible name the
line. The right column's top row is gone.

Refs plan #92, #1449
---
 frontend/src/ui/AGENTS.md                          |  2 +-
 frontend/src/ui/App.vue                            | 10 +++++++---
 frontend/src/ui/FileList.vue                       | 10 ++++++++--
 .../ui/{OperationBar.vue => OperationLabel.vue}    |  7 ++++---
 frontend/src/ui/operationText.test.ts              | 14 +++++++++++++-
 frontend/src/ui/operationText.ts                   | 13 +++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)
 rename frontend/src/ui/{OperationBar.vue => OperationLabel.vue} (59%)

diff --git a/frontend/src/ui/AGENTS.md b/frontend/src/ui/AGENTS.md
index 880baa4..76f64e6 100644
--- a/frontend/src/ui/AGENTS.md
+++ b/frontend/src/ui/AGENTS.md
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ Resizing (plan §2 #84): `ResizeDots.vue` draws the three dots of every resize h
 
 Questions (`asking.ts`): one at a time; `ask` resolves `"yes" | "no" | "dismissed"` (Escape is `dismiss`, a second `ask` while one waits is dismissed at once). Callers whose Escape means cancel compare `=== "yes"`. A question about the stop (`question.ts` `endsWithStop`: Mark resolved's, Abort's) is dismissed when the stop ends; the others stay.
 
-Listing and stops (plan §2 #87–#89): every list is `listing.ts` `refreshFiles` over `listStop`, the only writer of `files`, `operation` and `sideNames`, all from one reply; `MovedOn` goes to `nextStop`. `stops.ts` `nextStop` ends a stop: it bumps `latestOpen`, drops the stop (`saving.ts` `dropStop`: the `Stop` token marked dropped, every claim overtaken and gone), dismisses the stop's question, clears every per-stop state (opened files, choices, taken, notices, format notes, the shown file, the problem, git's stop message `stopMessage`, the screen) and lists as at start; `outside` with unsaved edits adds the one moved-on notice, `continued` to an empty stop the `stopped` problem and git's message as `stopMessage`, kept for the whole stop. "A reply after the stop was dropped changes nothing" is written once, `currentStop.ts` (`Stop`, `landed(stop, call)`: null once dropped): every write, the format step, Abort, Continue and every reload (`views.ts` `reload`, also for disk changes, `diskChanges.ts` `applyDiskChanges`) capture `target.stop` before they call. `StopMovedOn` always means the stop the window shows is gone (#1435): a list answered after it would only open the new stop under the old views, so every failure answered `StopMovedOn` — the writes, Abort, Continue, an open and every reload — goes once to `nextStop({ outside })` through `problem.ts` `reportFailure` (logged, no problem shown; its target asks only for `nextStop`), the one path. `operationText.ts` holds every operation word (the top line and its tooltip, Continue's and Abort's labels, Continue's hover, Abort's title and question); `OperationBar.vue` shows the top line above the notices while git records an operation.
+Listing and stops (plan §2 #87–#89): every list is `listing.ts` `refreshFiles` over `listStop`, the only writer of `files`, `operation` and `sideNames`, all from one reply; `MovedOn` goes to `nextStop`. `stops.ts` `nextStop` ends a stop: it bumps `latestOpen`, drops the stop (`saving.ts` `dropStop`: the `Stop` token marked dropped, every claim overtaken and gone), dismisses the stop's question, clears every per-stop state (opened files, choices, taken, notices, format notes, the shown file, the problem, git's stop message `stopMessage`, the screen) and lists as at start; `outside` with unsaved edits adds the one moved-on notice, `continued` to an empty stop the `stopped` problem and git's message as `stopMessage`, kept for the whole stop. "A reply after the stop was dropped changes nothing" is written once, `currentStop.ts` (`Stop`, `landed(stop, call)`: null once dropped): every write, the format step, Abort, Continue and every reload (`views.ts` `reload`, also for disk changes, `diskChanges.ts` `applyDiskChanges`) capture `target.stop` before they call. `StopMovedOn` always means the stop the window shows is gone (#1435): a list answered after it would only open the new stop under the old views, so every failure answered `StopMovedOn` — the writes, Abort, Continue, an open and every reload — goes once to `nextStop({ outside })` through `problem.ts` `reportFailure` (logged, no problem shown; its target asks only for `nextStop`), the one path. `operationText.ts` holds every operation word (the tag `operationTag`, the line `operationLine` and its tooltip, Continue's and Abort's labels, Continue's hover, Abort's title and question); `OperationLabel.vue` is the tag (plan §2 #92): `FileList.vue`'s last row under the list or tree while git records an operation, `App.vue` passing the store's `operation`; its hover is the line's tooltip, its accessible name the line.
 
 File marks (plan §2 #90): `FileMark.vue` renders a file's name and its mark in the list and the tree from one table per `FileStatus` (`Unresolved` none; `Resolved` the check and a muted name; `Remembered` the history icon with the rerere hint as its title and accessible name); `FileList.vue` and `FileTree.vue` pass only the status and the label.
 
